  "stock_photo": "https://bikebook.bikeindex.org/chase/2024/rsp-5-0-frame.jpg",
  "description": "IS THE CULMINATION OF THE REFINEMENTS AND UPGRADES TO MAKE IT OUR BEST ALLOY FRAME EVER!\n\nChase BMX started with the RSP 1.0 frame that Connor Fields rode from Day 1. Each time we updated the frame, we took the feedback from Connor, then Joris, and other Pro riders we sponsored. The RSP 5.0 is the culmination of the refinements and upgrades to make it our best Alloy frame ever.\n\nThe Chase RSP 5.0 Frames feature Tapered Headtube (Expert XL and above sizes), an Aero Seat Post tube, Enclosed Rear dropouts, Press Fit Bottom Brackets (Expert XL and Above), Triple and Double Butted tubes, Hydro and Muscle formed 7005 T6 Premium Ultralight tubing. RSP 5.0 Frames now feature a new internal cable routing from the Head Tube, through the Down Tube & Bottom Bracket, and exits out of the Chain Stay (Expert XL and Larger), and for the Mini – Expert, the cable exits out of the bottom of the down tube.\n\nAll Chase RSP 5.0 frames are Disc Brake only designed frames. The dropouts were restructured to offer better clearance for a wide array of disc brake calibers, improving the overall braking performance, and now compatible for both post and flat mount disc brake system (Disc Adapter kit sold separately).\n\nThe Chase RSP 5.0 Frame is now offered in a OS20 frame size option with refined geometry for riders wanting to use OS20 wheels, forks, and tires. OS20 uses the oversizes rims, tires, and forks to give larger riders a more comfortable ride as well as experience all the benefits of OS20.",
